    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on upgrading the security protocols for a mid-sized law firm. We're moving away from SMS-based MFA because of the interception risks and want to implement hardware security keys (like YubiKeys) instead. Can you give me a step-by-step guide on how to handle the deployment and the user onboarding process? We need it to be as seamless as possible so the partners don't complain.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Start by auditing your current authentication infrastructure to identify all systems requiring MFA, then procuring the necessary federal hardware security keys and setting up the FIDO2-compatible authentication node. Conduct parallel training sessions for all partners where each user physically tests their key on local trial instances to demonstrate the frictionless lock-in process. For the official rollout, schedule a window for live login testing alongside IT support staff who will be available in-person to assist with any unexpected hardware pairing issues. Implementing a clear, step-by-step internal help guide and celebrating early adopters will significantly reduce partner complaints and ensure a smooth transition away from SMS-based methods.",
